# Repository structure

Use the `src/` layout. Installable package lives at `src/cifar_cnn/`.

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `src/cifar_cnn/` | Application + ML library code only |
| `configs/` | Typed configs by concern (`data`, `model`, `train`, `serve`) |
| `scripts/` | Thin CLIs; no business logic |
| `tests/` | `unit`, `integration`, `contract`, `security`, `e2e`, `fixtures` |
| `docs/` | Governance, architecture, model cards, runbooks, evidence, implementation |
| `deploy/` | Docker, Kustomize overlays, Argo CD |
| `infra/terraform/` | Bootstrap + env stacks/modules |
| `models/` | Guide path for `cnn_model.pth` (weights gitignored) |
| `data/` | Local datasets; track manifests under `data/splits/` only |
| `artifacts/` | Local run outputs (gitignored) |
| `notebooks/` | Exploration only; never the production path |

## Rules

- Do not invent parallel top-level packages (`app/`, `backend/`, flat modules at root).
- Guide baseline artifacts stay at `models/cnn_model.pth` for Phase 5 compliance.
- Secrets never enter git; use `.env.example` templates only.
- Prefer edits inside the phase card's Allowed paths.
- Keep training code out of the final serving image unless explicitly required.
